      "side": 1,
      "message": "Boards with CONFIG_PLATFORM_EC_WP_EXTERNAL (USB FPMCU modules like sanok/et171 and chudow/ft9001) do not have a hardware WP GPIO pin (zephyr/Kconfig:1139-1141). Instead, write_protect_is_asserted() calls write_protect_is_asserted_external() in zephyr/drivers/wp/wp_external.c, which checks a C static bool \u0027unlocked \u003d false\u0027 in .bss RAM that is reset on boot/sysjump and is normally unlocked at runtime via the EC_CMD_FP_UNLOCK_DEV_OPTIONS host command (common/fpsensor/fpsensor_auth_commands.cc:255). Since there is no hardware GPIO pin for renode_ec_launch.py to toggle, system_is_locked_wp_off calls disable_write_protect_external() to put the external WP driver into the unlocked state. Updated the commit message and added an inline comment in PS 6 to clarify this.",
